(cooking oil) <put, in (cauldron)>
    <heat> ?= boiling
(cauldron) + (onions) 1head
(onions) <cook> ?= black
Discard the blackened onion.
(meat) <chop, coarsely>
(cauldron) + (meat)
(meat) <boil> ?= golden brown
(meat) + (salt) a pinch
(onions) <chop>
(cauldron) + (onions)
Wait 2 minutes.
(carrots) <slice>
(cauldron) + (carrots)
{mixture} <boil, another 2m>
{first tomato water} = (water) 500ml + (tomato paste)
(cauldron) + {first tomato water}
{mixture} <boil, 5m>
(long grain rice) <rinse>
    <put, into (cauldron)>
Do not mix.
{second tomato water} = (water) another 500ml + (tomato paste)
(cauldron) + {second tomato water}
{pilaf} <boil>
Reduce heat to minimum.
(cauldron) + (salt) 2tbsp
(cauldron) <close>
{pilaf} <cook, low heat; 1.5–2h>
Meanwhile [
    One hour before ready, or when water is no longer visible above the rice:
    {pilaf} + (garlic)
    If the rice is undercooked, turn it over now.
